# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 20 — Product Glossary

---

# Purpose

This glossary defines the official language of DigiSwasthya.

Everyone — product, design, engineering, support, QA, operations, and business stakeholders — must use these terms with the same meaning.

If a term is used differently in conversation than in this glossary, this glossary wins until the PDD is formally revised.

---

# A

## Acceptance Criteria
Measurable pass/fail statements used to audit whether the product matches the PDD.

## Active Connection
A Connection in Active status allowing trade between a Pharmacy and a Stockist.

## Admin / Platform Administrator
Platform governance user who verifies, suspends, supports, and monitors, but does not trade medicines.

## Allocation (Inventory)
Assignment/reservation of sellable stock (usually batch-level) to an order for fulfilment.

## Allocation (Payment)
Distribution of a payment amount across one or more invoices.

## Analytics
Derived insights calculated from source entities. Never the source of truth.

## Available Credit
Sum of remaining amounts on issued, non-expired, non-void credit notes for a trading pair.

## Available Inventory
On Hand quantity minus Reserved quantity for sellable batches.

## Audit Trail
Record of who did what, when, and what changed.

---

# B

## Batch
A manufacturing lot of a product with batch number, quantity, and expiry.

## Billable Quantity
Quantity eligible to appear on an invoice according to fulfilment/billing rules.

## Business
A legally registered organisation on DigiSwasthya operating as Pharmacy or Stockist.

## Business Verification
The process and record deciding whether a Business may trade.

## Buyer
In current product: the Pharmacy side of a trade.

---

# C

## Catalogue / Product Catalogue
The sellable list of products owned by a Stockist.

## Closed (Order)
Terminal operational status indicating the order lifecycle is finished under closure rules. Financial dues may still exist separately if policy allows operational close with open payables.

## Connection
Trading relationship between one Pharmacy and one Stockist.

## Counterparty
The other business in a trade relationship or transaction.

## Credit Note
Financial credit document issued by a Stockist reducing future/outstanding liability without rewriting historical invoice lines.

## Credit Remaining / Remaining Credit
Unapplied portion of a credit note.

---

# D

## Delivery
Entity representing transport of goods from Stockist to Pharmacy.

## Delivery Boy
Operational role that executes assigned deliveries.

## Disconnected
Connection status where prior relationship is closed and new trade is blocked.

## Dispatch
Act/state of sending packed goods out for delivery.

## Draft
Editable pre-submission state of an entity (order, invoice, payment, return, etc.).

---

# E

## Edge Case
Exceptional or conflicting situation requiring explicit product behaviour.

## Expiry
Date after which a batch is not sellable.

## Expiry %
Portion of shelf life consumed, when manufactury and expiry dates allow calculation.

## Export
Download/extraction of authorised dataset under permissions and filters.

---

# F

## Fill Rate
Delivered quantity relative to ordered quantity.

## Fulfilment
Stockist process of accepting, allocating, packing, dispatching, and delivering an order.

## Forbidden Transition
State change explicitly disallowed by the state machine.

---

# G

## GMV
Gross Merchandise Value — platform-level sum of non-void issued invoice totals for a period.

## GST
Goods and Services Tax applied per tax rules; may split into CGST/SGST or IGST.

## GSTIN / GST Number
Tax identity number of a business.

---

# H

## Hold (Payment On Hold)
Payment review state pausing approval/rejection pending clarification.

---

# I

## Inventory
Physical stock records for a business, maintained with batch-level movements.

## Invoice
Financial document defining what a Pharmacy owes a Stockist for billable goods.

## Issued (Invoice)
Invoice status where liability is officially created and lines are immutable in substance.

---

# L

## Lifecycle
Ordered progression of states an entity may pass through.

## Low Stock
Availability at or below reorder level.

---

# M

## Manager
Business operational role with broad permissions below Owner.

## Message
Conversational communication. Never an official approval mechanism.

## Movement (Inventory)
An auditable change in inventory quantity with reason/source.

---

# N

## Near Expiry
Batch within configured high-risk days-to-expiry bands.

## Net Sales
Gross sales minus credit notes issued in the period (per calculations).

## Notification
Event communication to users. Does not mutate business truth.

---

# O

## On Hand
Physical quantity held before subtracting reservations.

## Order
Purchase request from Pharmacy to Stockist. Intent to buy; not itself settlement.

## Order Line
A product + quantity (+ price snapshot and related fields) within an order.

## Outstanding / Outstanding Balance
Amount still due on an invoice or across invoices after approved payments and applied credits.

## Owner
Primary business controlling role with full business administration rights including ownership transfer.

---

# P

## Pack / Packed
Fulfilment state where goods are prepared for dispatch.

## Partial Delivery
Delivery of some but not all expected goods.

## Partial Fulfilment
Supplying only part of requested order quantities under rules.

## Payment
Record of money paid by Pharmacy toward invoice liabilities.

## Pharmacy
Buyer business that purchases from stockists.

## Platform
DigiSwasthya system and its governance layer.

## Product
Sellable medicine/healthcare item listed by a stockist.

## Product Definition Document (PDD)
The master non-technical specification of what DigiSwasthya is and how it must behave.

---

# Q

## Quarantine
Batch/inventory status making stock non-sellable pending disposition.

---

# R

## Recall / Recalled
Safety status blocking sellable allocation/distribution of a batch.

## Recipient (Notification)
User/business inbox target for an event notice.

## Rejected
Terminal negative decision state for requests (order, connection, payment, return, verification, etc.).

## Reorder Level
Threshold at or below which low-stock status appears.

## Reserved Inventory
Quantity committed to fulfilment and unavailable for new allocation.

## Return
Request to send back delivered goods for approval and potential credit.

## Role
Primary business type role (Pharmacy/Stockist/Admin) or internal operational role (Owner/Manager/Staff/Delivery Boy/Accountant).

---

# S

## Settlement
Process of reducing outstanding liability via approved payments and applied credits.

## SKU
Stock keeping unit / stockist product code identity for a catalogue product.

## Source of Truth
Authoritative entity record from which derived data is calculated.

## Staff
Internal business user role with limited operational permissions.

## State Machine
Definition of legal states and transitions for an entity.

## Stockist
Seller/distributor business that supplies pharmacies.

## Support Ticket
Assistance request to platform support; does not itself mutate trade documents.

## Suspended
Business/user status that blocks operational access/trade while retaining history.

---

# T

## Tax Snapshot
Tax rate/amount captured for a line at the governing commitment point.

## Trade / Trading
Ordering, fulfilment, invoicing, payment, and related B2B commerce actions between connected verified businesses.

## Transition
A legal move from one entity state to another by an allowed actor.

---

# U

## User
Individual person account belonging to exactly one Business.

---

# V

## Validation
Pre-commit checks preventing illegal inputs or states.

## Verification
See Business Verification.

## Void
Controlled cancellation of a financial document under strict rules, retaining audit record.

---

# W

## Wishlist / Save for Later
Pharmacy-saved products not yet ordered.

---

# Term Distinctions (Critical)

## Order vs Invoice
Order = purchase intent/fulfilment request. Invoice = financial liability document.

## Payment vs Settlement
Payment = submitted/approved money record. Settlement = effect on outstanding after approval/allocation.

## Return vs Credit Note
Return = physical/request workflow. Credit Note = financial credit document after approval/adjustment.

## Notification vs Message
Notification = event alert. Message = conversation. Neither is an official approval.

## Available vs On Hand
On Hand = physical stock. Available = On Hand − Reserved (sellable).

## Business vs User
Business owns records. User acts on behalf of one business.

## Analytics vs Source Records
Analytics summarise. Invoices/orders/payments remain authoritative.

## Disconnect vs Suspend
Disconnect ends a pair’s trading relationship. Suspend blocks a business platform-wide (governance).

## Draft vs Issued
Draft editable. Issued financial documents are substantive records.

